\title{The Shape of a Proof System}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}
\meta{toc}{true}

\p{
    The vocabulary layer. [FRI](dhsorens-0037), [Spartan](dhsorens-003G), and [WHIR](dhsorens-003C) are instances of the same handful of definitions, and much of what is confusing in a paper is a confusion about which definition is in play: [which soundness notion](dhsorens-002F), in which oracle model, against which adversary.
}

\p{
    Two questions this section exists to answer. What does a security proof for a SNARK actually establish? And at which step of the compilation from interactive protocol to deployed system does the security get lost?
}

